		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Physics Engine Programmer @ Ubisoft Bucharest]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=38344#p38344"><![CDATA[
<strong class="text-strong">Ubisoft Bucharest </strong>is looking for a <strong class="text-strong">Physics Engine Programmer </strong>who will research and develop new features and tools requested by AAA games (Assassin's Creed, The Division, Steep, Ghost Recon and many other unannounced titles).<br><br>The engine’s name is <strong class="text-strong">Motion</strong> and it is a <strong class="text-strong">real time physics engine </strong>able to simulate soft and rigid bodies.<br><br><strong class="text-strong">Your responsibilities</strong><br>•Participate in the design and development of APIs &amp; tools <br>•Ensure clear and structured programming, keeping performance, maintenance and compatibility requirements in mind<br>•Collaborate with game development teams to help integrate the SKD and tools in their production pipeline<br>•Correct the bugs determined by other working units and the quality control team<br><br><strong class="text-strong">Your profile</strong><br>•Highly experienced in C++ programming<br>•Good knowledge of algorithms and OOP<br>•Strong 3D math skills<br>•Knowledge of (game) physic will be a plus<br>•Good knowledge of C# and WPF will be a plus<br>•Bachelor’s degree in computer science or computer engineering or equivalent<br>•Good spoken/written English<br>•Ability to work as part of a team with excellent communication &amp; interpersonal skills<br><br><strong class="text-strong">We offer:</strong><br>•Professional working environment<br>•Relocation assistance <br>•Access to private medical system<br>•Meal tickets <br>•Fully featured Gym, large Cafeteria, relaxation area, bike rental service<br>•Access to most of our games up to date for research and fun<br><br>Let’s get in MOTION!<br><br>We look forward to receiving your application at <a href="mailto:roxana.busuioc@ubisoft.com">roxana.busuioc@ubisoft.com</a>.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=11896">Ubisoft</a> — Wed Oct 19, 2016 2:28 pm</p><hr />
